Subject: Add EnoSpellCheck flag: mark keys apply to non-Vietnamese syllables (SpellCheck=off, DdAnywhere)

bamboo-core has no way to turn the syllable validity gate off. EnoSpellCheck
skips isValid in findMarkTarget and the uow shortcut; tone placement is unchanged.
Apply with: patch -p1 < this file (from the bamboo-core dir).

--- a/bamboo.go
+++ b/bamboo.go
@@ -33,6 +33,8 @@
 	// EautoRestore restores the raw keys of a non-Vietnamese word (windows, text, Linux)
 	// when a word-break key (space, punctuation, digit) is typed after it.
 	EautoRestore
+	// EnoSpellCheck lets mark keys (aa, ow, dd...) apply even when the syllable is not Vietnamese.
+	EnoSpellCheck
 	EstdFlags = EfreeToneMarking | EstdToneStyle | EautoCorrectEnabled
 )
 
--- a/bamboo_utils.go
+++ b/bamboo_utils.go
